==Description== <!--T:2-->

<!--T:3-->
The [[Image:Sketcher_MergeSketches.svg|24px]] [[Sketcher_MergeSketches|Sketcher MergeSketches]] tool merges two or more sketches.

==Usage== <!--T:4-->

<!--T:5-->
# Select two or more sketches.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Sketcher_MergeSketches.svg|16px]] [[Sketcher_MergeSketches|Merge Sketches]]}} button (not available in the [[PartDesign_Workbench|PartDesign Workbench]]).
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Sketch → [[Image:Sketcher_MergeSketches.svg|16px]] Merge Sketches}} option from the menu.
# A new sketch is created.

==Notes==

{{Version|26.3}}:
* If all selected sketches belong to the same [[PartDesign_Body|Body]], the merged sketch is created inside that Body. Otherwise it is created at the document level.
* [[Sketcher_Projection|External geometry]] is imported when its source object belongs to the same document and Body as the merged sketch. Objects outside any Body can be referenced when the merged sketch is also outside any Body. References already present in the merged sketch are reused.
* Constraints that use imported external geometry are transferred to the corresponding references in the merged sketch. External geometry outside the permitted scope is skipped, together with constraints that depend on it. Check the [[Report_View|Report View]] for messages about skipped geometry or constraints.


